This will be a semi-short version since I ascended a while ago.  I
prefer wizards for the "fun" difficult early game.  I am thoroughly
spoiled and had a near ascension experience with a previous wizard,
sacrificing on the wrong altar.  That was disappointing....  Anyhow I
was pretty proud of the conducts for this first real ascension.

Lyric started out only OK as starts go.  The 16 Int was not the
greatest.  Some equipment was notable, though including a wand of
speed, wand of tele and an early wand of polymorph.  My starting cat,
Snowflake, became a fast leocrotta that tore everything up.  The first
few levels also had a co-aligned altar and a couple of shops to rob,
so the early game was made a bit easier.  I did sokoban first and
received AoR.  Along the way I picked up a dog, Teddy, though I didn't
poly him because I wanted to keep some of those charges and Snowflake
was plenty strong.

The mines were pretty easy.  In the first few levels I found a BoH,
which was quite nice.  I also ran across a unicorn that donated it's
horn - the first of many.  Mine town was the grotto version, which I
find very annoying.  The guards were no match for my pets and I
quickly bought the protection I was after.  The priest went bye-bye
when my pets showed up and after gaining some levels I converted the
altar and sac'd for Magicbane.  I also max'd my stats with blessed !
oGA and got lucky with a full inventory blessed ID that answered a few
remaining questions.  Normally I would go back up to the main dungeon
and develop/explore a bit more but with MR, reflection, Magicbane and
strong pets I was pretty confident.  That's where the problems start!

Mine's end (the Wine Cellar) would have been easy except a MMF sucked
my brains upon entering.  I should have engraved E but I didn't -
typing too fast.  It cost me some maps and lots of IDs that were not
easy to replace.  I didn't have the spell ID having only recently
gotten lucky with a blessed scroll.  That really hurt and reminded me
how easy it is to get careless.  Normally I would have geno'd liches
and MFs at this point but I wanted to try a genoless conduct, which I
managed to keep all the way through.

On my way back up, luckstone in hand, I found a poly trap and my pets
became a black dragon and an Olog-hai.  These pets were pretty much
unstoppable and that left me free to level up for the quest.  I also
up'd my luck through sac'ing and received vorpal.  At this point I had
to decide between a full on sac fest for death drops or doing the
quest and claiming the very nice prize at the end.  The Dark One is a
wimp so I proceeded to the quest.  It was generally uneventful, except
that the Dark One had a WoD that took out Snowflake.  I really like
keeping my first pet and an Olog-hai, especially with a silver sabre
and full armor, is a very durable companion.  Rest in peace
Snowflake.  My prize, though, the AoE, was well worth it.

What I really wanted now was SDSM and I had an idea.  I had a ring of
polycontrol and a WoP, so I made myself into a silver dragon and laid
about 16 eggs.  I was also missing SR so I poly'd into a blue dragon
and laid one egg.  Then I let myself die while CMing food for my
brood.  Eventually my babies starting turning into adults.  I pestered
the adults with rocks while wearing a ring of aggrevate monster.
Quickly my adult pets became enemies and were cut down by my remaining
pets.  After about eight corpses, some scales finally dropped.  I also
ate the blue dragon corpse for SR.  Yea, killing and eating your
babies doesn't sound too "neutral" but it worked and didn't require a
wish.  I kept the AoR on for double reflection goodness.  That was
fortuitous because later my black dragon, Teddy, went feral in Soko
and would have disintegrated me.  My SDSM was off after an incubus
"encounter"...  YASD avoided.

After getting SDSM I dug out DL 12 for a major sacfest.  It was quite
an undertaking but the finished product was a sacfest palace.  I
managed my luck to avoid crowning and received lots of golden glows,
protection points and spellbooks.  I used my wand of poly and some
collected cloaks and boots to fill out my kit.  Coming out I had a
HoB, GoD, all the boots and other armor I needed and -50 AC.  I
collected a lot of death drop potions which I alchemized with the rest
of my stash for !oFH and (un)holy water.

Above my sac palace I used some water demons to build a nice harem of
foocubi and that was my main method to gain lvls, HPs and PW.  So pre
medusa and pre castle I had a lvl 30 fully decked out wiz with 800
power and lots of spells (including MM).  The rest was just a cake
walk.  I destroyed Ludios, Medusa and the Castle.  I stashed the wand
and then zoomed through to Vlad using magic mapping and controlled
tele.  Once I had that branch available through AoE, I ported back to
my Soko stash and consolidated my gear.  There was a lot I didn't need
anymore and some things that I wanted, like FA.  I poly'd for that and
poly'd my horns, spellbooks and lots of other stuff hoping for some
random cool items and spells.  Magic markers were really tough to come
by in this game.  That polypiling episode was the first time that
conflict showed up.  I held onto the ring but avoided using it.  At
this point I felt ready to ascend and invoked my way back to Vlad and
continued on.

The demons were easy, though Orcus dodged a lot of FoD blasts and his
wand was empty when I looted it.  Rodney went down to FoD also.  I
used the cursed tele trick for the sanctum, detect unseen to find the
entrance, FoD for the priest then !GL'd out.  Lots of mysterious
force.  The planes were easy - I had lots of tele wands for air
elementals.  Astral wasn't too bad.  I had several scrolls of charging
to boost my PW when it got low.  Pesty and Death showed up near the
entrance.  Both died quickly to FoD and MM respectively.  I was
massively over prepared with AoLS, !FHs and the like so astral was
anti-climatic.  The second altar proved to be neutral.  Next stop, the
demi-god saloon for a well earned martini stirred gently with my
unused WoW (0:3).



